      "writtenOn": "2016-03-04T00:45:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Mostly being sarcastic. We have been in this constant struggle between flexibility and standardization. With Keystone v3, in theory, an endpoint is not limited to \"admin\", \"public\", or \"internal\". One can also define a \"foo\" interface. But that won\u0027t work with some of the existing clients out there. Now that we are in the standardization mode, I suspect we will only be recognizing those three going forward. See\n\nhttps://review.openstack.org/#/c/181393/17/specs/service-catalog.rst\n\nline 171",
      "parentUuid": "7af24918_adeae671",
      "revId": "caf3c369516d7c86da2fef57e0b5dc0867428012",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
